# GMS counts the damage-over-time effects the character's own skills have
# alight on the enemies in front of them and pays 3% final damage apiece, up to
# five of them. The burns are real now, and the fight can count them, so it is
# the count rather than the flat 15% it used to be.
#
# A count over the GROUP, which is what "within a certain range" means: eight
# monsters carrying one burn each are eight. So it stands at its cap on a map
# and pays only what the rotation keeps alight on a boss -- and at 2nd job,
# where Poison Breath is the only thing that burns, hardly at all. GMS says so
# in as many words.
name: "Elemental Drain"
skill_order: 2
description:
  "Increases your Final Damage for each continuous damage effect your skills "
  "have on nearby enemies."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_WIZARD
max_level: 10
dot_count_cap: 5
base { final_dmg_pct_per_dot: 0.003 }
per_level { final_dmg_pct_per_dot: 0.003 }
